WEBVTT

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:04.230
I consider this a serious source of concern!

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:09.500
In a time when humanity should focus 
on bringing together all its knowledge,

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:14.810
a mistaken mindset is threatening the noble 
purpose behind the Prominence Project!

00:00:14.810 --> 00:00:17.240
And this mindset is pervasive 
in the Blue Flag exercises!

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:22.640
The Eishi participating in the exercises 
are obsessed with victory over one another,

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:25.540
and have come to view 
each other as the enemy!

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:33.460
And so I have come up with a plan 
to put an end to this foul trend!

00:00:33.770 --> 00:00:38.760
These violent impulses should be curbed 
in a productive and healthy manner!

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:41.020
And the person to make this happen is you!

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:43.420
Lt. Takamura!

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:53.070
<b>Deep Green</b>

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:32.560
What? Are you still mad?

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:37.380
Isn't this the time to think about 
how we take out those stealth jerks?

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:38.460
But...

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:41.340
Nothing we can do. It's 
already been decided.

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:46.220
We can't confirm any plans we 
come up with in a simulator.

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:47.530
This sucks.

00:02:47.530 --> 00:02:50.100
Well, that's true of all the other teams, too.

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:56.170
That's why Ibrahim is staying behind 
and running strategy simulations.

00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:01.610
An international friendship meeting?

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:08.370
All Test Flights will begin at their 
designated points and march on foot to Point Alpha.

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:13.050
The army will be providing reward money, 
with more going to the teams who get there first.

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:19.160
Security squads and other support groups will also 
head to Point Alpha when their mission is complete.

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:23.890
Afterwards, the international 
friendship meeting.

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:26.900
It will take place in the buffer zone 
between the base and USSR territory.

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:29.600
It will begin in 48 hours.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.400
Any questions?

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:35.400
Why have the groups participating 
in Blue Flag do this now?

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:42.150
To put it simply: To put an end to the 
growing rivalry between the different research groups.

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:47.300
Sure, the betting's been getting 
a little out of hand lately.

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:50.900
The mechanics are the ones doing 
the betting, make <i>them</i> go!

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:52.410
Why do we Eishi have to go?

00:03:53.050 --> 00:03:58.670
The number of fights between Eishi in Lilifort 
has been rising rapidly since the exercises began.

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:02.740
The way Blue Flag is pitting the 
various countries against each other

00:04:02.740 --> 00:04:07.220
is probably driving the Eishi's 
nationalism, is my guess.

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:08.900
I see.

00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:12.940
We've always had a lot of countries in 
our squad, so I didn't really notice.

00:04:14.140 --> 00:04:17.900
And that's the reason that 
Lieutenant Orson came to us.

00:04:18.580 --> 00:04:20.940
Lt. Orson?

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:25.560
Argos, with its Eishi from many nations, serves 
as a model of what the Prominence Project should be.

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:28.370
And it should be the team to 
win this propaganda mission.

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:29.450
Is what he says.

00:04:30.050 --> 00:04:31.580
Live up to his expectations.

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:33.460
That is all. Dismissed.

00:04:36.180 --> 00:04:41.410
Victory in Blue Flag is the only 
way to keep the XFJ project going,

00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:44.460
and silence those who think production 
should be done domestically.

00:04:45.610 --> 00:04:49.960
I'm more focused on victory than anyone here.

00:04:50.460 --> 00:04:52.200
What's wrong, Yuuya?

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:53.980
You've just been staring out the window.

00:04:54.420 --> 00:04:56.020
Oh, yeah.

00:04:56.640 --> 00:05:01.480
It feels like it's been a 
long time since I came here.

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:11.200
That's right.

00:05:25.490 --> 00:05:28.510
Command Post to Argos 1: Check in.

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:31.760
This is Argos 1. We've passed checkpoint 3.

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:34.520
Marching towards objective.

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:36.400
Command Post, roger.

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:39.800
Ensign Bridges, do your best 
and get there first, okay?

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:42.520
We can't get there second?

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:46.730
If you were willing to go out to 
a nice dinner in Lilifort with me,

00:05:46.730 --> 00:05:48.610
I might be a little more motivated.

00:05:48.610 --> 00:05:54.540
Huh? Ensign Giacosa, didn't you 
just tell me the same thing?

00:05:54.880 --> 00:05:56.340
Me too.

00:05:56.340 --> 00:05:58.100
Oh, no-no-no.

00:05:58.100 --> 00:06:00.570
Of course, all of you at the same time.

00:06:00.570 --> 00:06:05.410
Everyone, Ensign Giacosa says he's going to 
throw a party for us when he gets back to base.

00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:08.260
Wait, what?

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:10.640
We're still on mission. That's enough.

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:12.880
That's right, Lieutenant!

00:06:12.880 --> 00:06:15.600
Tell those hyenas to calm down-

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:18.420
We'll handle the details of the party here.

00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:20.860
You can relax and focus on your mission.

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:24.900
Huh? Lt. Takamura?

00:06:25.210 --> 00:06:26.660
Argos 1, roger.

00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:28.730
That was really nice of you, VG.

00:06:30.220 --> 00:06:33.050
Well, it's only if we're 
the first ones there.

00:06:33.050 --> 00:06:36.160
You dummy. That stopped mattering 
about halfway through the conversation.

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:38.300
Seriously?

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:40.980
Then we have to be #1 no matter what.

00:06:41.720 --> 00:06:45.500
Anyway, Princess Yui's really 
softened up hasn't she?

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:49.170
Yeah. Not too long ago she would've 
been yelling and screaming.

00:06:50.320 --> 00:06:51.160
That's true.

00:06:55.500 --> 00:06:58.020
Well, I'm sure a lot's happened with her too.

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:02.690
Christ. He doesn't have a clue.

00:07:06.240 --> 00:07:06.930
If Yu-

00:07:08.530 --> 00:07:11.200
If Ensign Bridges comes to 
us with an emergency call me.

00:07:14.130 --> 00:07:16.180
I'm going to get the refreshments ready.

00:07:16.180 --> 00:07:17.860
You take care of the rest.

00:07:17.860 --> 00:07:21.840
If you're handling it, I'd like 
some more meat and potato stew!

00:07:21.840 --> 00:07:23.690
I'd like it curry-style.

00:07:23.690 --> 00:07:26.460
All the Eishi from around the 
world will be very happy!

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:28.710
Will they?

00:07:30.530 --> 00:07:34.090
I-If it can contribute to 
humanity coming together,

00:07:34.090 --> 00:07:35.420
I'll give it serious consideration.

00:07:36.260 --> 00:07:37.660
Nice thought there.

00:07:37.660 --> 00:07:39.680
That'll give the Lieutenant her excuse.

00:07:40.010 --> 00:07:41.300
Yeah.

00:07:41.300 --> 00:07:45.420
But you know, she's really 
wasted on that blockhead.

00:07:45.420 --> 00:07:47.340
If I could I'd like to marry her.

00:07:47.780 --> 00:07:52.200
Lt. Takamura is cooler and 
more handsome than most guys.

00:07:56.170 --> 00:07:59.410
You're my bride, princess!

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:01.560
Oh, you silly girl.

00:08:01.560 --> 00:08:04.500
Hey, don't forget about Lida too!

00:08:06.360 --> 00:08:07.130
I like it.

00:08:07.640 --> 00:08:09.000
Like what?

00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:14.050
This is kind of nice.

00:08:14.890 --> 00:08:16.010
What brought this on?

00:08:16.380 --> 00:08:20.220
I was just thinking that I never paid much 
attention to nature, or anything like that.

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:24.020
I just blew right past it.

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:28.770
When something's always around you, you 
don't realize what it's worth until it's gone.

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:31.530
Always around you...

00:08:37.040 --> 00:08:37.900
Hey!

00:08:39.420 --> 00:08:40.500
Something smells.

00:08:42.890 --> 00:08:43.920
Something's there.

00:08:49.010 --> 00:08:52.050
Damn, I hope it's not a grizzly.

00:08:52.050 --> 00:08:56.540
Capturing or killing wild animals goes 
against the rules of the mission.

00:09:00.530 --> 00:09:01.620
This is Argos 1.

00:09:01.960 --> 00:09:03.420
We're almost at Point Alpha,

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:06.000
but there's a chance we've 
encountered a large wild animal.

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:07.440
Requesting permission to open fire on it.

00:09:08.010 --> 00:09:08.890
Roger.

00:09:08.890 --> 00:09:13.320
Permission granted, but only if 
warning shots don't scare it off.

00:09:13.700 --> 00:09:15.140
Argos 1, roger.

00:09:23.100 --> 00:09:25.770
The smell's getting stronger. 
They're chasing us.

00:09:26.280 --> 00:09:27.000
They're here?

00:09:28.820 --> 00:09:30.850
We're at a disadvantage in the forest.

00:09:30.850 --> 00:09:33.140
We need to concentrate our 
fire in an open area!

00:09:33.460 --> 00:09:34.800
Right in front of us. Let's go.

00:09:45.580 --> 00:09:46.730
Split up and surround it.

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:55.900
What are you doing?

00:09:56.370 --> 00:09:57.400
You too!

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:06.000
What is this strange voice?

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:07.910
The smell's coming from over there.

00:10:12.050 --> 00:10:13.240
Let's go, Leon.

00:10:13.240 --> 00:10:13.840
Roger.

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:37.340
Huh?

00:10:37.340 --> 00:10:38.290
A hot springs?

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:43.100
You...

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:53.360
Definitely.

00:10:53.760 --> 00:10:56.710
I can't believe there's a natural 
hot springs all the way out here.

00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:02.360
So this is definitely Point Alpha.

00:11:02.360 --> 00:11:04.470
That was nice of Lt. Orson.

00:11:05.020 --> 00:11:07.600
Sending us newlyweds to 
a hot springs honeymoon.

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:09.280
Right, darling?

00:11:09.640 --> 00:11:10.980
Whoo-whoo!

00:11:11.780 --> 00:11:14.170
We're not newlyweds and 
this is not our honeymoon.

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:20.130
They're staring into each other's eyes again.

00:11:21.440 --> 00:11:22.530
We are not!

00:11:22.810 --> 00:11:24.880
Getting along nicely, I see.

00:11:24.880 --> 00:11:27.000
Maybe fate is bringing us together.

00:11:28.130 --> 00:11:30.610
They were partners once, after all.

00:11:32.410 --> 00:11:33.360
Yuuya!

00:11:35.810 --> 00:11:37.930
You walked through the 
forest, just the two of you?

00:11:38.300 --> 00:11:39.450
Where's the rest of the Test Flight?

00:11:39.850 --> 00:11:42.530
We're the only ones who came here.

00:11:42.530 --> 00:11:45.840
I see. You must be tired 
after walking so many hours.

00:11:45.840 --> 00:11:49.050
Nope, I walk a lot so I'm okay.

00:11:49.740 --> 00:11:51.290
That's true, come to think of it.

00:11:55.640 --> 00:11:57.320
Inia, is something wrong?

00:11:57.320 --> 00:11:58.980
I don't know!

00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:05.060
Would you like to use our equipment 
until your support teams get here?

00:12:06.460 --> 00:12:07.690
No, but...

00:12:08.090 --> 00:12:11.060
She's not used to walking through 
the forest. She must be tired.

00:12:11.530 --> 00:12:13.600
At this rate she'll catch cold.

00:12:14.010 --> 00:12:15.500
That's...

00:12:15.770 --> 00:12:16.750
What do you want to do, Inia?

00:12:17.440 --> 00:12:20.560
If I'm with Cryska, plus Yui 
and Yuuya are there too...

00:12:22.500 --> 00:12:23.570
Alright.

00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:25.510
Well... Thank you very much.

00:12:25.970 --> 00:12:26.530
No problem.

00:12:28.980 --> 00:12:30.930
Wait a second!

00:12:31.890 --> 00:12:35.210
What do you think you're doing, inviting 
another girl out in front of your bride?

00:12:35.210 --> 00:12:36.850
Wait, who's supposed to be my bride?

00:12:37.290 --> 00:12:39.610
Me, who else!

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:41.220
Yuuya...

00:12:41.220 --> 00:12:42.640
Nice job, boss!

00:12:42.640 --> 00:12:44.360
Nice punch.

00:12:44.360 --> 00:12:46.610
I don't understand at all...

00:12:46.930 --> 00:12:49.330
Would you stop that already?

00:12:49.330 --> 00:12:52.140
Why don't you stop trying 
to sleep around then?

00:12:52.140 --> 00:12:54.280
Hey, want to go join the fun?

00:12:52.210 --> 00:12:54.290
Bridges, what is "sleeping around"?

00:12:55.080 --> 00:12:56.620
I'm tired of this!

00:12:55.090 --> 00:12:56.620
Why do I have to hang out with him?

00:12:56.960 --> 00:12:58.440
Lt. Takamura!

00:12:58.440 --> 00:13:01.240
Sorry to bother you when you're busy,

00:13:01.240 --> 00:13:03.410
but would it be alright if we joined you?

00:13:03.410 --> 00:13:06.730
Of course, go ahead Lt. Blazer!

00:13:06.730 --> 00:13:09.640
I've prepared traditional Japanese 
cuisine as well, why don't you try some?

00:13:09.980 --> 00:13:11.640
How wonderful!

00:13:13.040 --> 00:13:16.040
You anxious to try some 
traditional Japanese cuisine?

00:13:17.480 --> 00:13:19.560
Well, I'll admit it.

00:13:19.940 --> 00:13:22.660
You're such a naughty boy.

00:13:22.660 --> 00:13:24.300
What are you talking about?

00:13:24.300 --> 00:13:27.300
That's the problem with closet 
perverts who are narcissists.

00:13:27.300 --> 00:13:29.090
Shut up, Chobi.

00:13:49.420 --> 00:13:51.850
So this is the full version 
you were telling me about?

00:13:52.340 --> 00:13:55.350
Yes. I boiled it for 
several hours this time.

00:13:57.340 --> 00:13:58.500
What's wrong, Yuuya?

00:13:58.930 --> 00:14:01.380
No, it just reminded me of home.

00:14:02.540 --> 00:14:06.360
My mom used to make this a 
lot, before she passed away.

00:14:06.660 --> 00:14:08.000
I see.

00:14:08.690 --> 00:14:12.520
This stew was a favorite of 
my dad before he passed away.

00:14:14.360 --> 00:14:15.120
I see.

00:14:22.560 --> 00:14:24.560
My dad must've liked it too.

00:14:26.060 --> 00:14:27.370
This smells good!

00:14:27.560 --> 00:14:29.220
Ensign Sestina!

00:14:29.570 --> 00:14:30.550
Want to try some?

00:14:30.960 --> 00:14:31.620
Yeah!

00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:38.640
The potatoes taste good, don't they?

00:14:55.340 --> 00:14:58.060
Everyone, dinner's ready!

00:14:58.060 --> 00:15:00.410
Your wife's delicious mabo tofu is ready!

00:15:01.460 --> 00:15:04.490
You'd rather have me than the food?

00:15:04.490 --> 00:15:07.020
No, not here in public!

00:15:08.040 --> 00:15:09.290
Is something wrong?

00:15:09.290 --> 00:15:11.570
This is food, right?

00:15:13.240 --> 00:15:14.460
How rude.

00:15:14.460 --> 00:15:17.530
Everyone who tried it loved 
it so much they passed out.

00:15:17.530 --> 00:15:18.060
See?

00:15:20.780 --> 00:15:23.320
It's obviously fatal!

00:15:24.650 --> 00:15:27.680
Love can overcome any danger!

00:15:27.680 --> 00:15:29.690
So you admit there's danger?

00:15:30.100 --> 00:15:31.780
Are you two friends?

00:15:33.240 --> 00:15:35.300
A ranking officer is 
being very kind to you.

00:15:35.300 --> 00:15:37.700
Why don't you try it, Ensign Bridges?

00:15:39.060 --> 00:15:39.780
Here!

00:15:46.760 --> 00:15:48.050
Yahoo!

00:15:51.020 --> 00:15:52.300
This is nice.

00:15:52.650 --> 00:15:53.680
Jeez.

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:55.800
It's not a pool!

00:15:56.060 --> 00:15:57.530
That's right, Ensign.

00:15:57.850 --> 00:16:00.130
You're supposed to have your 
swimsuit accidently fall off,

00:16:00.130 --> 00:16:02.560
and then say "You pervert!"

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:07.640
Okay, everyone.

00:16:07.640 --> 00:16:10.070
The kind thing to do is ignore her.

00:16:10.970 --> 00:16:12.570
Wait, before that!

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:15.580
Why did everyone bring a swimsuit?

00:16:17.560 --> 00:16:19.240
I'm terribly sorry.

00:16:19.240 --> 00:16:21.920
Lt. Orson insisted we not tell you.

00:16:22.220 --> 00:16:24.040
What?

00:16:24.040 --> 00:16:28.180
Japanese tradition says you go 
in a hot springs naked, right?

00:16:28.180 --> 00:16:30.300
Don't get embarrassed now.

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:33.280
The water's nice, Lieutenant. Come in.

00:16:40.450 --> 00:16:41.560
This is wonderful.

00:16:42.530 --> 00:16:46.570
I never thought I'd find such a splendid 
hot springs all the way out here in Alaska.

00:16:51.450 --> 00:16:52.570
Go!

00:16:54.040 --> 00:16:54.950
What are you doing?

00:16:55.300 --> 00:16:56.580
Huh?

00:16:56.580 --> 00:17:00.700
Isn't it bad manners to get in a hot 
springs with a towel on in Japan?

00:17:07.940 --> 00:17:10.130
I've finally gotten used to the smell.

00:17:10.530 --> 00:17:14.590
Now then, I need to get my skin 
all nice and soft for Yuuy-

00:17:15.480 --> 00:17:17.930
So that's how you're gonna play it?

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:19.600
Not bad, princess.

00:17:19.970 --> 00:17:20.970
Then...!

00:17:23.960 --> 00:17:25.770
Way to go, boss!

00:17:25.770 --> 00:17:28.620
They're a pretty close match, 
except for their boobs.

00:17:28.620 --> 00:17:31.270
I really don't understand this.

00:17:33.560 --> 00:17:35.730
So you're getting desperate, huh?

00:17:35.730 --> 00:17:39.100
Looks like you're no ordinary princess.

00:17:40.650 --> 00:17:43.620
That lieutenant is pretty cute, you know?

00:17:43.620 --> 00:17:44.570
Right?

00:17:44.570 --> 00:17:45.840
So's Yuuya.

00:17:47.010 --> 00:17:48.290
What, Stella?

00:17:48.290 --> 00:17:50.520
Why are you being friendly 
with the stealth girl?

00:17:51.300 --> 00:17:53.210
Just doing some information gathering.

00:17:53.490 --> 00:17:55.180
How scary.

00:17:55.180 --> 00:17:56.520
Go soft on me.

00:18:01.890 --> 00:18:06.620
The lieutenant must be pretty bold if 
she's going into a hot springs naked.

00:18:06.620 --> 00:18:10.480
No, I think this was a conspiracy...

00:18:11.050 --> 00:18:12.890
But is this okay?

00:18:12.890 --> 00:18:16.320
The men's hot spring has been 
kind of noisy for a while now.

00:18:16.320 --> 00:18:17.880
We're fine,

00:18:17.880 --> 00:18:19.740
but if the men came peeking those two...

00:18:20.300 --> 00:18:22.380
It'd be fine if it were Yuuya.

00:18:22.680 --> 00:18:23.240
Wh-

00:18:23.530 --> 00:18:25.420
Oh, don't worry about that.

00:18:25.780 --> 00:18:26.690
It's fine.

00:18:30.610 --> 00:18:34.250
Damn it. Paradise is right in front of us!

00:18:34.700 --> 00:18:37.210
When did you get here?

00:18:37.210 --> 00:18:38.860
It's a big wave!

00:18:38.860 --> 00:18:40.760
We've gotta try and ride it.

00:18:41.380 --> 00:18:42.530
But...

00:18:42.530 --> 00:18:43.970
Is this the end?

00:18:45.330 --> 00:18:46.620
Don't give up!

00:18:46.970 --> 00:18:48.520
If we fall here...

00:18:48.860 --> 00:18:51.180
Who will carry on their dreams?

00:18:52.380 --> 00:18:53.540
VG!

00:18:56.660 --> 00:18:58.860
You sure that's enough muscles?

00:18:59.260 --> 00:19:02.460
No problem!

00:19:04.520 --> 00:19:06.870
Hey, stop...

00:19:07.460 --> 00:19:09.040
I'm not fated to die here...

00:19:09.040 --> 00:19:10.500
Beautiful, aren't they?

00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:11.920
My pecs.

00:19:16.250 --> 00:19:19.760
Did you just hear something 
from the men's hot springs?

00:19:20.120 --> 00:19:22.730
Tarisa, don't worry about it.

00:19:26.060 --> 00:19:29.090
So they lasted 12 minutes and 
45 seconds against Gairos?

00:19:29.540 --> 00:19:32.140
Not bad, Argos Flight.

00:19:33.100 --> 00:19:35.320
What are they doing?

00:19:41.010 --> 00:19:42.980
This is kind of nice.

00:19:44.290 --> 00:19:45.530
Yuuya!

00:19:46.130 --> 00:19:47.530
Yuuya!

00:19:50.290 --> 00:19:50.750
Go!

00:19:55.050 --> 00:19:57.050
Inia, what are you doing here?

00:19:57.050 --> 00:19:58.460
I wanted to take a bath with you!

00:19:58.890 --> 00:20:00.900
Where's your swimsuit?

00:20:00.900 --> 00:20:01.980
I didn't bring it.

00:20:02.480 --> 00:20:05.390
I didn't know you were that bad.

00:20:06.760 --> 00:20:08.260
Wait! You've got it all wrong!

00:20:10.090 --> 00:20:11.450
So he has special tastes, huh?

00:20:12.360 --> 00:20:13.020
This...

00:20:13.900 --> 00:20:14.850
This sucks.

00:20:15.740 --> 00:20:16.580
Yuuya?

00:20:16.920 --> 00:20:18.620
There you are, Inia.

00:20:18.620 --> 00:20:20.300
Oh, Cryska.

00:20:20.600 --> 00:20:21.650
Can you take Inia and-

00:20:27.180 --> 00:20:28.800
You-

00:20:31.260 --> 00:20:32.210
No!

00:20:33.250 --> 00:20:34.640
C-Cryska?

00:20:40.740 --> 00:20:42.800
What am I...

00:20:43.240 --> 00:20:44.130
I'm sorry!

00:20:46.660 --> 00:20:47.720
Let's go, Inia.

00:20:53.240 --> 00:20:54.410
Cryska?

00:21:00.810 --> 00:21:03.110
What was that just now?

00:21:12.720 --> 00:21:14.980
I can't believe this!

00:21:16.130 --> 00:21:20.100
You went over to the guys' 
area? What are you thinking?

00:21:20.420 --> 00:21:22.080
It doesn't have anything to do with you.

00:21:22.080 --> 00:21:23.180
What?

00:21:23.970 --> 00:21:26.130
I didn't think of that.

00:21:48.650 --> 00:21:50.530
Looks like it was a good break.

00:21:52.730 --> 00:21:55.120
The day of the Infinities 
fight has been decided.

00:21:58.260 --> 00:21:59.120
You're all ready, right?

00:21:59.520 --> 00:22:00.460
Yes sir!

00:22:02.130 --> 00:22:04.400
Let's finish this, Leon.

00:23:37.500 --> 00:23:41.880
As you requested, the entirety of 
the outdoors mission was filmed.

00:23:42.280 --> 00:23:42.940
Good.

00:23:43.410 --> 00:23:45.940
I see you've recorded every last bit of it.

00:23:46.740 --> 00:23:49.610
Even if it is for the 
UN's propaganda efforts,

00:23:49.610 --> 00:23:53.040
I never want to be a part of 
a mission like this again.

00:23:56.540 --> 00:23:58.700
That's just fine!

00:24:07.160 --> 00:24:09.040
Next time will be a special episode.

00:24:09.040 --> 00:24:11.170
We'll be looking back on 
what Argos has done so far,

00:24:11.170 --> 00:24:14.400
as well as shining light on incidents 
not directly discussed in the show.

00:24:14.400 --> 00:24:17.420
There'll be new TSFs, and changing 
relationships between the players.

00:24:16.760 --> 00:24:24.350
<b>Total Eclipse: Before the Climax SP</b>

00:24:17.420 --> 00:24:19.760
And lots of information as 
we head into the climax.

00:24:19.760 --> 00:24:23.820
As well as a pre-broadcast of the 
footage for the new opening and ending.

00:24:23.820 --> 00:24:25.820
Look forward to it.
